# KISS & DRY

## KISS (Keep It Simple)

- Prefer **one obvious path** over configurable frameworks (e.g. in-process job run vs HTTP wake + cron + retry UI).
- Do not abstract until the **second** justified use — inline first copy; extract on repeat.
- Avoid extra layers (wrapper services, generic handlers) that only pass data through.
- Server actions: validate → call one application use case → revalidate — no orchestration soup in UI files.

## DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself)

- Duplicate **behavior** (auth checks, org scoping, error mapping) → extract to `lib/` helper or application use case.
- Duplicate **markup** (second copy in UI) → extract atom/molecule per [`atomic-design.mdc`](atomic-design.mdc).
- Do **not** DRY unrelated code that merely looks similar — coupling unrelated features hurts more than duplication.

## Where helpers live

| Concern | Location |
|---------|----------|
| Org/role access checks | `lib/*-access.ts` (delivery) |
| Business rules | `src/core/domain/` |
| Use-case orchestration | `src/core/application/` |
| UI composition | atoms → molecules → organisms |

## Anti-patterns

- Copy-pasting `findMeetingByIdForOrg` + seller check in every action — use shared access helper.
- Mega-components doing fetch + auth + layout + feature logic — split template vs organism.
- "Utility" modules importing React and Prisma together.
